The SIF's smaller size and lower GDP allocation reflect Okaiken's strategic choice to invest in technological sophistication and physical culture integration rather than mass mobilization. This approach produces a military that is highly capable within its defensive mission but lacks the power projection capacity of larger forces — a deliberate trade-off consistent with the Kurosawa Doctrine.

